// Title: Defrag Deactivation
// Sigma ID: 958d81aa-8566-4cea-a565-59ccd4df27b0
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Bartlomiej Czyz (@bczyz1)
// Date: 2019-03-04 | Modified: 2022-10-09
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, execution, persistence, T1053.005, S0111
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects the deactivation and disabling of the Scheduled defragmentation task as seen by
//   Slingshot APT group
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://securelist.com/apt-slingshot/84312/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules-emerging-threats/2018/TA/Slingshot/proc_creation_win_apt_slingshot.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\schtasks.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/delete" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/change") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/TN" and ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Defrag\\ScheduledDefrag")
